From: aurtxx <aurtxx@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] hook: bypass Setup Wizard blocker and suppress failing system OTA engine

On first boot, Google's Setup Wizard blocks progression at OtaStatusFragment:
"System update failed" with error status 0x713.

Root Cause:
update_engine expects a 12.88 GB dynamic super partition with dual A/B slots
(/dev/block/by-name/boot_a). In gbOS86 live/USB installs, the system is backed
by a linear read-only 3.68 GB EROFS super image booting via systemd-boot.
Consequently, update_engine permanently fails verification and blocks setup.

This patch:
1. Adds `gbos_provision` to init.rc: automatically injects `device_provisioned 1`,
   `user_setup_complete 1`, disables `setupwizard`, `SystemUpdateActivity`,
   `SystemUpdateService`, and stops `update_engine`.
2. Mask update_engine service definitions in Android init by bind mounting
   an empty file over `/new/system/etc/init/update_engine.rc` and
   `/new/system/etc/init/update_engine_sideload.rc`.

--- a/gbos/hook.sh
+++ b/gbos/hook.sh
@@ -381,6 +381,7 @@
     write /sys/kernel/tracing/tracing_on 0
     $TRUSTYSTOP
+    start gbos_provision
     start gbos_audiodiag
     start gbos_devname
     start gbos_iptsd
@@ -440,6 +441,14 @@
+service gbos_provision /system/bin/sh -c "for i in 1 2 3 4 5; do settings put global device_provisioned 1 && settings put secure user_setup_complete 1 && settings put global ota_disable_automatic_update 1 && pm disable com.google.android.setupwizard && pm disable com.google.android.desktop.setupwizard && pm disable com.google.android.gms/.update.SystemUpdateActivity && pm disable com.google.android.gms/.update.SystemUpdateService && stop update_engine && stop update_engine_sideload && break; sleep 2; done"
+    user root
+    group root
+    seclabel u:r:shell:s0
+    oneshot
+    disabled
+
 # Logical display size (RESOLUTION in gbos.cfg); "reset" = native 1920x1080.
 service gbos_wmsize
@@ -701,6 +710,9 @@
 # apgetty (UART shell) has no UART configured here and crash-loops
 : > /tmp/empty.rc && mount --bind /tmp/empty.rc /new/system_ext/etc/init/apgetty.rc && log "hook: apgetty disabled"
+for rc in /new/system/etc/init/update_engine.rc /new/system/etc/init/update_engine_sideload.rc; do
+  [ -f "$rc" ] && mount --bind /tmp/empty.rc "$rc" && log "hook: $(basename $rc) disabled"
+done
 log "hook: kvm: $(ls /sys/class/misc | grep -E 'kvm|vhost' | tr '\n' ' ')"
